Rule 1 (input and other tensors must be broadcast-compatible across all dims)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 2 (neither input nor other tensor may have a complex dtype)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 4 (out with two tensors: must be bool dtype and match the broadcasted shape)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ((shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))
